Short:        MintAMP 2.0 development player
Author:       Darren Banfi (boingball)
Uploader:     boingball@gmail.com (Darren Banfi)
Type:         mus/play
Version:      2.0-dev
Requires:     68030+; TCP/IP for radio; AmiSSL for HTTPS; ReAction or GadTools
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

MintAMP 2.0 development - PR #521
================================

Use the MintAMP-2.0-dev-68030 or MintAMP-2.0-dev-68060 drawer appropriate to
your processor. Keep its decoder modules and Skins drawer with the players.
This is a development build awaiting real-hardware acceptance.

Double-click MintAMP-Launch for the default native ReAction interface.
Use Project / Interface preferences to select ReAction or GadTools and
Native or Classic skin for subsequent launches through MintAMP-Launch.
The running decoder is left alone; no live frontend switch is required.
You can also run MintAMP-Launch --prefs from a Shell.

The launcher icon includes disabled examples of these ToolTypes:
  (GUI=REACTION)
  (MODE=NATIVE)
  (SKIN=PROGDIR:Skins/MintAMP-mintleaf.wsz)
  (DOUBLESIZE=NO)

Remove parentheses to force a setting. Explicit CLI arguments override
ToolTypes, which override saved preferences, which override defaults.
Leave examples disabled for the saved GUI/appearance preferences to work.

The bundled mint-leaf skin opens by default when the skinned appearance is
selected. Load skin from the player's menu to change it. Spectrum and MP3 EQ
are optional and initially off. Native utility windows remain accessible.

The four original launch methods remain available:
  MintAMP       Native ReAction       MintAMP-GT   Native GadTools
  MintAMP-SR    Skinned ReAction      MintAMP-SGT  Skinned GadTools
  amiga_mp3dec.fastexp                Command-line player

Details: Skins/ReadMe, docs/winamp-skins.md and the hardware acceptance checklist.
No Winamp Windows DLL plug-ins, modern WAL skins or all-format biquad EQ.

Made by Darren Banfi / boingball, with Helix MP3/AAC, libfoxenflac,
ESP8266Audio and Tremor. Existing licences and decoder credits apply.
Support: https://buymeacoffee.com/boingball
